# No trailing slash, and that is load-bearing (MAX-81). A `dir/` pattern only matches a real
# directory, and git does not follow symlinks, so `node_modules/` ignored the installed tree but
# did not ignore a symlink named node_modules -- which is how an absolute host path
# (/home/opc/math-training-app/node_modules) ended up committed to main as a 120000 entry and
# reproduced by `git archive` for every operator's clean export. Bare `node_modules` matches both.
node_modules
dist/
build/
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
artifacts/
.data/
# The compiled Figure.jsx the degraded-state test imports. It is deleted when the suite finishes,
# and ignored so that a suite killed halfway does not leave a build product in a commit.
web/test/.degraded-*/
# The report `check-content-math.mjs --json --selftest` wrote to a file literally named
# `--selftest`, because `--json` took the next argv token as its output path (MAX-97). The parser
# rejects a value beginning with `-` now, so this name cannot be produced by that call again. It is
# ignored rather than deleted on sight because the defect is a shape -- any tool that takes a bare
# path will do the same thing to the next flag -- and a name git already knows about is one fewer
# stray report to find on main later. The file itself is untracked as of MAX-97.
--selftest
